Guest module: src/amk/amk_guest.c holds the guest handle's make side: variable reads and
writes, eval, the queue a forked guest's writes ride up, the collector, $(goal), and
$(amk.stdin). This patch is make's side of the move: the moved code leaves function.c and
the object joins the build. Every name it shares was global already.

amk_call stays in function.c with amk_function_exists, since it is the bridge into make's
own function table: it reads lookup_function, expand_builtin_function and func_call, which
stay static.

